01:06:31,428 --> 01:06:37,428
Maverick is a 1994 American Western comedy film directed by Richard Donner,
and starring Mel Gibson, Jodie Foster, and James Garner.

12
01:12:34,285 --> 01:12:40,285
The screenplay by William Goldman, based on the 1957–1962 television series of the same name created by Roy Huggins and originally starring
Garner, stars Gibson as Bret Maverick, a card player and con artist who collects money to enter a high-stakes poker game.

13
01:18:37,142 --> 01:18:43,142
He is joined in his adventure by Annabelle Bransford (Foster), another
con artist, and Marshal Zane Cooper (Garner), a lawman.

14
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:46,000
The supporting cast features Graham Greene, James Coburn, and Alfred Molina, and many cameo
appearances by Western film actors, country music stars, and other actors.

15
01:30:42,857 --> 01:30:48,857
Maverick was filmed from August to December 1993.

16
01:36:45,714 --> 01:36:51,714
Released theatrically by Warner Bros.

17
01:42:48,571 --> 01:42:54,571
on May 20, 1994, the film was both a critical and commercial success,
grossing $183 million worldwide against a $75 million budget.

18
01:48:51,428 --> 01:48:57,428
It was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Costume Design.

19
01:54:54,285 --> 01:55:00,285
The film explores themes of ship, saloon, poker,
mississippi river, native american.

20
02:00:57,142 --> 02:01:03,142
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
